 "final_summary": "The bug was that retry_call was retrying all exceptions without checking their type. The fix added a check to only retry on exceptions specified in the retry_on parameter, ensuring non-transient errors like ValueError are not retried. This aligns with the expected behavior that only retry_on errors are retried.",
 "diff": "diff --git a/tracker/retry.py b/tracker/retry.py\nindex c12947e..bc11126 100644\n--- a/tracker/retry.py\n+++ b/tracker/retry.py\n@@ -24,7 +24,9 @@ def retry_call(func, attempts=3, base_delay=0.05, sleep=time.sleep, retry_on=(Tr\n     for attempt in range(attempts):\n         try:\n             return func()\n-        except Exception:\n+        except Exception as e:\n+            if not isinstance(e, retry_on):\n+                raise\n             if attempt == attempts - 1:\n                 raise\n             sleep(delays[attempt])\n",
